// Function: proto_num(name) → Int | null
//
// IANA protocol number for a transport-layer protocol name. The
// universal mapping used by every vendor parser that needs to fill
// `connection_info.protocol_num` on an OCSF record.
//
// Accepts both lowercase and uppercase forms — Zeek emits `"tcp"`,
// Junos / Palo Alto / Sysmon / Suricata emit `"TCP"`, Check Point
// mixes both. `lower()` collapses the case difference before lookup
// so callers do not need to know the upstream's convention.
//
// Returned value: IANA protocol number (per RFC 5237 / IANA's
// "Assigned Internet Protocol Numbers" registry). `null` for any
// name not in the set below — keeps the call site OCSF-safe (a
// missing protocol_num is preferable to a wrong one).
//
// Coverage scope: the transport / encapsulation protocols that real
// security telemetry sources actually emit on `proto`:
//
//   tcp     → 6     (RFC 9293)
//   udp     → 17    (RFC 768)
//   icmp    → 1     (RFC 792)
//   icmpv6  → 58    (RFC 4443)
//   sctp    → 132   (RFC 9260)
//   gre     → 47    (RFC 2784)
//   esp     → 50    (RFC 4303 — IPsec encapsulating security payload)
//   ah      → 51    (RFC 4302 — IPsec authentication header)
//
// Out of scope (return null): OSPF, IGMP, IPv4/IPv6 encapsulated,
// EtherIP, PIM, etc. Add when a vendor parser surfaces them.
//
// Used by: parse_zeek_*, parse_suricata, parse_checkpoint_*,
// parse_juniper_srx_*, parse_paloalto_*, parse_sysmon (any parser
// emitting OCSF 4001 Network Activity or a class with
// connection_info.protocol_num).

def function proto_num(name) {
    switch lower(name) {
        "tcp"    { 6 }
        "udp"    { 17 }
        "icmp"   { 1 }
        "icmpv6" { 58 }
        "sctp"   { 132 }
        "gre"    { 47 }
        "esp"    { 50 }
        "ah"     { 51 }
        default  { null }
    }
}
